<h1 style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:800;">Custom Domains</h1>
<p>Brand your short links with your own domain instead of using <code>go.utmpro.link</code>.</p>
<h2>Adding a Custom Domain</h2>
<ol>
    <li>Go to <strong>Links → Domains</strong> in your workspace</li>
    <li>Click <strong>+ Add Domain</strong></li>
    <li>Enter your domain (e.g., <code>links.yourbrand.com</code>)</li>
    <li>Create a CNAME record in your DNS pointing to the target hostname shown</li>
    <li>Wait for verification (automatic, checked every 5 minutes)</li>
</ol>
<h2>DNS Configuration</h2>
<pre>Type:  CNAME
Name:  links (or your subdomain)
Value: [CNAME target hostname - shown in the add domain dialog]
TTL:   300</pre>
<h2>Domain Limits by Plan</h2>
<table><tr><th>Plan</th><th>Custom Domains</th></tr>
<tr><td>Free</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Pro</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>Business</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>Advanced</td><td>50</td></tr></table></div>
<h2>Managing Domains</h2>
<p>You can edit a domain's default redirect URL, add a description, or delete it from the Domains page. System domains (like <code>go.utmpro.link</code>) are managed by the administrator and cannot be edited by users.</p>
